# BootGaps-1 (lane BootGaps, 2026-10-30): ONE eager run before each CUDA graph capture (graphs.capture), was two.
# Every GLM capture site (decode one-stream Graphs: main/sparse/MTP; verify.BatchedVerify.capture; dflash2.Drafter.capture;
# dflash2_multi.MultiDrafter.capture) ran its graph body eagerly twice before capturing it. None of the bodies changes
# host state a later call reads (parities are set by the caller before each capture; positions, extents, tables are
# device tensors), so the second eager run leaves every recorded launch as the first did. Boot only; replies unchanged.
# Boot estimate from run-20261029-185803: P=1 one-stream graphs 234 x ~44 ms eager window (calibration's eager v1) ~= -10 s
# of the 27.8 s phase; P=2/4 BatchedVerify 64 graphs (94 ms a graph incl. 2 warm-ups) ~= -2 to -3 s of the 11.1 s
# MultiDecoder phase; P=6/8 128 graphs ~= -4 to -6 s of 17.1 s. Test: test_one_warmup.py (GPU). Applies with patch -p0.
